@startuml
!include theme.puml
title Leave | Self-service request, segregated decision and notification
autonumber
actor "Employee\nstaff UI" as E
participant "HR API" as HR
database hr_db as DB
actor "HR approver\nadmin/super-admin API" as A
E -> HR : POST leave/requests + bearer token
HR -> DB : Find employee by verified user_id
HR -> HR : Validate end >= start
HR -> DB : INSERT pending LeaveRequest; COMMIT
HR --> E : 201 pending request
A -> HR : POST leave/requests/{id}/decision
HR -> DB : Fetch tenant request + employee
alt Not pending
  HR --> A : 409 Already decided
else Approver is the request employee
  HR --> A : 403 No self-approval
else Authorized different approver
  group One transaction
    HR -> DB : Set approved/rejected + actor/time
    opt Employee has linked identity user
      HR -> DB : INSERT Notification(user_id, message)
    end
    HR -> DB : COMMIT
  end
  HR --> A : Decision response
end
E -> HR : GET notifications/mine
HR --> E : User-scoped in-app records
E -> HR : POST notifications/{id}/read
HR -> DB : Check ownership; set read_at once; COMMIT
HR --> E : Updated notification
note over E,A
Employee UI exists; decision UI does not.
Notifications are fetched, not email/SMS/push messages.
No timer-driven notification polling is configured in the current UI.
Concurrent decision serialization is a separate acceptance test.
end note
@enduml
